				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## AST walk and alias merging\n\nEvery Elixir coder runs {{gtMethod:name=ElixirFunctionExpanderStyler>>style:ast:}} on each source change. After attaching inline `|>` expander triangles, it calls `attachUnknownModuleWrenchesIn:source:`. That pass parses the source locally with SmaCC `ElixirParser` (cached per source-hash on the styler instance, so the parse cost amortizes over keystrokes), collects every `ElixirDotAliasNode`, drops the heads of `defmodule` / `defprotocol` blocks (the module being defined, not referenced), and keeps only outermost spans.\n\nAlias merging happens in {{gtMethod:name=ElixirFunctionExpanderStyler>>extractAliasesFrom:}} - a line-scan of `alias` directives including the grouped form `Foo.{A, B, C}` (parsed by `parseGroupedAliasBody:`). The inline `|>` editor (whose source is just a function body) needs the enclosing module's aliases too; those come from a bridge call to `GtBridge.Analysis.module_aliases/1` and merge with the source-extracted ones (source wins on conflict)."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-29T19:31:04.416657+08:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-29T19:31:04.416657+08:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "84lDmbYJSe2xiLgxPw0LBA=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Batched bridge query\n\n{{gtMethod:name=BeamModuleResolution>>classify:}} answers `#resolved` / `#unresolved` / `#unknown` purely from local sets. The `#unknown` names from one source change get batched into one bridge call to `GtBridge.Analysis.modules_loaded?/1`, which reads `Analysis.LoadedModules` (an ETS set populated from `:application.get_key/2` and maintained additively by EventBroker `%ModuleEvent{}` events). Results land back in the cache via `recordResolved:unresolved:`.\n\nAfter warm-up the unknown set is empty and the styler bridges zero times per source change. The first keystroke after a fresh image is the only one that pays the round-trip."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-29T19:31:15.261368+08:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-29T19:52:03.736054+08:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "UrEuwhSCSHaF6oeqVw7K1Q=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## The wrench attribute\n\nFor each `#unresolved` span the styler attaches an {{gtClass:name=ElixirUnknownModuleAttribute}}: a `BrTextAdornmentDynamicAttribute beAppend; stencil:` wrapping a wrench `BrButton` (`BrGlamorousVectorIcons repair`). Append-mode means the icon sits one char past the end of the identifier instead of replacing the trailing letter. Click it to see the \"Create module\" dropdown - that dispatches to `GtBridge.ModuleCreator.create/1` and rides the standard recompile-and-fanout path; {{gtClass:name=BeamModuleResolution}} hears the event on the wildcard channel, moves the name from `unresolved` to `resolved`, and the next style pass renders no wrench.\n\nThe Elixir snippet below has one resolved reference (`String`) and one made-up unresolved one (`Nope.Missing`) - the wrench should sit on the second:"
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-29T19:31:40.686417+08:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-29T19:31:40.686417+08:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "JVGbQ2FFSqeGQfH+U29u4A=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## End-to-end example\n\nTwo snippets that exercise the full pipeline. First, classify a name we know doesn't exist:"
