				"code" : "\"Build a styler over a tiny source string referencing one known module\n and one unknown one. Inspect the returned attributes - exactly one\n wrench should be attached, on the unresolved span.\n\n (BEAM-side end-to-end coverage lives in lib/examples/e_module_creator.ex.)\"\nsource := 'String.upcase(\\\"hi\\\")\nNope.Missing.boom()'.\nstyler := ElixirFunctionExpanderStyler new.\n{ #classifyOne -> (BeamModuleResolution default classify: 'String').\n  #classifyTwo -> (BeamModuleResolution default classify: 'Nope.Missing').\n  #stylerClass -> styler class name }"
